From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RTL8812AU Mesh Project <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 23:44:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] wifi: rtw88: admit RTL8812AU USB mesh interfaces

RTL8812AU can operate as a standalone mac80211 mesh point, but rtw88 does
not advertise that interface type. Enable it only for the tested RTL8812A
USB path and only when mac80211 mesh support is built.

Current wireless-next already honors FIF_OTHER_BSS independently. It also
installs interface combinations only for RTL8822C, so no filter or
combination change is needed here.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
index cd92543..8150297 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
@@ -2286,6 +2286,10 @@ int rtw_register_hw(struct rtw_dev *rtwdev, struct ieee80211_hw *hw)
 	hw->wiphy->interface_modes = BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION) |
 				     BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP) |
 				     BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_ADHOC);
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MAC80211_MESH) &&
+	    rtwdev->chip->id == RTW_CHIP_TYPE_8812A &&
+	    rtw_hci_type(rtwdev) == RTW_HCI_TYPE_USB)
+		hw->wiphy->interface_modes |= BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT);
 	hw->wiphy->available_antennas_tx = hal->antenna_tx;
 	hw->wiphy->available_antennas_rx = hal->antenna_rx;
 
